<h2>7. Your rights</h2>
<p>Under the GDPR you have the right:</p>
<ul>
	<li>of <strong>access</strong> to your personal data and information about its processing (Art. 15);</li>
	<li>to <strong>rectification</strong> of inaccurate or incomplete data (Art. 16);</li>
	<li>to <strong>erasure</strong> (“right to be forgotten”) where the conditions are met (Art. 17);</li>
	<li>to <strong>restriction</strong> of processing (Art. 18);</li>
	<li>to <strong>data portability</strong> of the data you provided, in a structured, machine-readable format (Art. 20);</li>
	<li>to <strong>object</strong> to processing based on legitimate interest (Art. 21);</li>
	<li>not to be subject to a decision based solely on automated processing (Art. 22) – no such processing takes place.</li>
</ul>
<p>
	Rights are exercised by a written request to the contact details in section 1. A response is provided
	without undue delay and at the latest within one month, which may be extended by two further months where
	necessary, with notice. Exercising your rights is free of charge, except for manifestly unfounded or
	excessive requests.
</p>
<p>
	The rights to erasure and to object may be limited where processing is necessary for compliance with a legal
	obligation of the attorney or for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims.
</p>

<h2>8. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
<p>If you believe your rights have been infringed, you may lodge a complaint with the Bulgarian Commission for Personal Data Protection (CPDP):</p>
<ul>
	<li>Address: 2 Prof. Tsvetan Lazarov Blvd., 1592 Sofia, Bulgaria</li>
	<li>Website: <a href="https://www.cpdp.bg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.cpdp.bg</a></li>
	<li>Email: kzld@cpdp.bg</li>
</ul>
<p>We would appreciate the opportunity to address your concerns directly first.</p>

<h2>9. Data security</h2>
<p>
	Appropriate technical and organisational measures are applied to protect personal data against unauthorised
	access, loss or disclosure: encrypted connection (HTTPS), restricted access to correspondence and
	compliance with attorney–client confidentiality under the Bulgarian Bar Act.
</p>

<h2>10. Mandatory or voluntary provision</h2>
<p>
	Providing data through the form is voluntary. Without a name, contact details and a description of your
	matter, however, we cannot respond to your enquiry.
</p>

<h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>
	This policy may be updated when legislation or our processing practices change. The current version is
	published on this page with the date of the last update.
</p>
